{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787323364334993001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"shaggy-crass-bull","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e5daf383300f8df77fd32b1ba69154f8bbcdbc0d2b7d1c29e698875139a875d2","event_uuid":"282b9e56-c137-4b64-80b8-f0b2369f7a18","position":{"commit_sha":"7207027c4fe31ce10ba2e7f2d60010b34a91d266","position":"1787320693786502001-282b9e56-c137-4b64-80b8-f0b2369f7a18"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fa502efec8cf5244bb8d44f9e5fbb57fa576a7a8f3b568a51e9136efd5959fcd","event_uuid":"dd5ec2a1-778d-46cb-abe4-464b0f156062","position":{"commit_sha":"6f4903d53cb98fbf6f1d42e081ef7be0c5ac288d","position":"1787320710221078001-dd5ec2a1-778d-46cb-abe4-464b0f156062"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787320693786502001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dd5ec2a1-778d-46cb-abe4-464b0f156062","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"43d4-b8f5-4bb2-417b"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nThree defensive `except`/`isinstance` arms that decide whether an LLM-tier failure ABORTS or\nDEGRADES have **no test that reaches them**. Found by the Step-7 parity sweep while fixing bug\n`wolflike-chevroned-haddock` (`43d4-b8f5-4bb2-417b`).\n\nDemonstrated by mutation: reverting each arm to its pre-fix form leaves the **entire** unit\nsuite green.\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` mid-run plan-review arm (~:189) and mid-run\n  code-review arm (~:522). These `try` blocks have no broad `except`, so an escaping error\n  loses the `gate_error_v1` sidecar and the degraded-verdict contract. A probe driving\n  `produce_plan_review_verdict` with a runner whose `preflight` passes and whose `run` raises\n  could not reach either arm — the workflow executor absorbs the failure into the\n  finders-failed tail first — and that is true for the **pre-existing** `LLMUnavailableError`\n  too, so this is not a gap introduced by 43d4. It is unclear from outside whether these arms\n  are reachable at all; if they are not, they are dead code and should be removed rather than\n  maintained.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/container_stage.py` warm-call abort (~:209). `container_stage`\n  has **zero** referencing tests, so the whole module's abort-vs-degrade decision is unpinned.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThese arms encode cost and fail-closed rulings (abort rather than fan out N-1 doomed calls;\nnever degrade a blind run into a clean result). An unpinned ruling silently stops holding the\nnext time the exception vocabulary moves — which is exactly what bug 43d4 was.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A test reaches `gate_dispatch`'s mid-run plan-review arm and asserts the degraded verdict\n      plus the emitted `gate_error_v1` sidecar — or, if the arm is proven unreachable, it is\n      removed and that removal is recorded with the evidence.\n- [ ] The same for the mid-run code-review arm.\n- [ ] A test drives `container_stage`'s warm-call path and asserts the abort, so reverting the\n      `isinstance` arm turns it RED.\n- [ ] Each new test is shown to FAIL when its arm is reverted (a recorded mutation check), not\n      merely to pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c72a-48be-054d-4005","ticket_type":"task","title":"Untested mid-run/warm-call fail-closed arms in gate_dispatch and container_stage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["282b9e56-c137-4b64-80b8-f0b2369f7a18","dd5ec2a1-778d-46cb-abe4-464b0f156062"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787323364334993001,"uuid":"e2bd4e52-6435-44e9-bb0b-b01bb423c0d3"}